 {"id":"fabro-bfe1","title":"Qualitygate: add a loop-asset tier with a checked-in evidence-smoke.nu regression","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:47:40.355Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T20:07:45.753Z","description":"Run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X: the tester's 'just qualitygate' ran 4.15s with 'no crates touched / format clean' — zero machine verification of the actual changes (evidence.nu, reviewer.md). Verification fell to the two costliest LLM stages: implementer hand-built a scratch-git exercise (216s inference) and the reviewer re-ran it (57s), then the regression exercise was deleted at closeout. Change: in the qualitygate recipe (justfile / scripts/qualitygate.nu) add a loop-asset tier — a 'nu -c source' check for .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/*.nu plus a checked-in mixed-capture scratch exercise as evidence-smoke.nu following the existing closeout-smoke.nu pattern. Effect: deterministic verification of loop-asset changes, durable regression coverage, fewer manual-verification turns. Distinct from fabro-50f8 (prompt-mandated ad-hoc exercises) and fabro-574d (crate derivation): gate infrastructure plus a durable checked-in regression. Basis: run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X, workflow version c25ec2416a5e45108d80b6ea43ca9f9e394a3f8fab9ed6d0e53cfa2d3e45bdfa, commit 592f64bd92615069d6a7dbf32cc98c75eabb74e6","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-09T20:07:45.753Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-c49c","title":"Close the gate-ban equivalence loophole in planner step 7","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T20:14:39.400Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T20:22:22.759Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 7, extend the gate-command rewrite rule from matching only 'just qualitygate' to also matching its recipe body or equivalent invocation (per PROJECT_FACTS the recipe delegates to 'nu scripts/qualitygate.nu'); the permitted substitute stays gate-green via the deterministic tester step. In run 01M23W4S7Q2GNEVPY779M4GMN6 the planner rewrote the banned command into its byte-equivalent body (checkpoint seq 82, justfile:128), so the implementer and reviewer each ran the full gate on top of the tester — three gate executions on one tree. The prior fix (fabro-f7cf, closed) only matched the literal command name; this is the bypass of that implemented rule, a different mechanism. Expected effect: no redundant full-gate runs; on Rust-touching seeds each avoided run is a cold compile measured at 8-15 min. Cross-references: fabro-f7cf (prior, implemented). Basis: run 01M23W4S7Q2GNEVPY779M4GMN6, workflow version 38bab0b8b1faad62aaddb5e68facf6f1c58286169676479d3edbf99d4205b91c, commit 4c8683243f8c295438cf019e2f061f8812fc58db","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-5e3c","title":"Fix hardcoded cwd restore in evidence-smoke.nu","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T20:14:45.326Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T20:22:22.837Z","description":"In scripts/evidence-smoke.nu (~line 60), replace the hardcoded 'cd /workspace/fabro' cwd restore with a captured $env.PWD at script start. The reviewer in run 01M23W4S7Q2GNEVPY779M4GMN6 found this defect (journal seq 296) and approved anyway because the only channel was a full Changes-requested cycle; the smoke was checked into the gate by seed fabro-bfe1's new loop-asset tier and now executes in every future 'just qualitygate', misbehaving in any worktree checkout. Expected effect: the new gate tier stays green outside the canonical checkout path, and the latent break stops executing on every run. Cross-references: fabro-bfe1 (open — added the tier that checked this script into the gate; thematic overlap, not the same change). Basis: run 01M23W4S7Q2GNEVPY779M4GMN6, workflow version 38bab0b8b1faad62aaddb5e68facf6f1c58286169676479d3edbf99d4205b91c, commit 4c8683243f8c295438cf019e2f061f8812fc58db","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-afb8","title":"smoke.nu uses 'get -o' which nushell 0.101 rejects — weblab deploys fail the smoke recipe although the server is healthy","status":"in_progress","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T20:32:25.962Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-10T08:26:02.500Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"Weblab deploy 2026-09-09 ~20:40Z: 'just up' completed fully (image built, CLI 0.348.0 installed, compose recreated fabro-fabro-1, wait-healthy green twice) but the recipe then FAILED at scripts/smoke.nu:91 with a PARSE error: 'The get command doesn't have flag -o' on 'open $auth_path | get -o servers | default {}'. The weblab HOST nushell is 0.101.0 (just invokes the host nu; the mise nushell 0.115.0 pin lives only in the run toolchain image) while the dev machine that authored/tested smoke.nu runs nu 0.115.0, where get -o/--optional exists. Result: every weblab deploy reports failure while the deployment actually succeeded — the deploy ceremony cannot trust its exit code. Wanted: make smoke.nu (and audit the other nu deploy scripts: wait-healthy.nu, install-cli.nu) compatible with the OLDEST supported host nu, or have the justfile invoke the pinned nushell explicitly. 0.101-compatible form for the failing line: 'get -i servers | default {}' (-i/--ignore-errors exists in 0.101) or a try/catch wrapper. Acceptance: 'nu --ide-check'-level parse of smoke.nu under 0.101 semantics (or a smoke run against a 0.101 host); deploy on weblab exits 0. Basis: weblab ~/deploy-20260909.log tail (parse error + 'Recipe smoke failed'), weblab nu --version 0.101.0, dev-machine nu 0.115.0, manual smoke after the failure (ps ok, auth probe 200, container healthy).","labels":["workflows"]}
